# L §5.17 Lots (round 16, the fresh critic: HOLE-LOTS split from HOLE-ANCHOR): "Lots held before the run are observed
# acquisitions dated before the start (§5.19), each with its value and day, which a fill binds and nothing books; the
# opening reading at the start anchors their sum (`HOLE-LOTS` when they disagree, §8.1)"; L §8.1 HOLE-LOTS: `<place>:
# the lots held before <S> sum to <a>, the opening reading states <b>`. p1 (4 glb) and p2 (6 glb) are held before
# 2026-01-01, 10 glb, against an opening of 12 glb: each lot is that hole, and so is each take of it (t1; L §5.12
# Holes: a hole side makes the take a hole). The balance stands on the opening reading: 12 - 5 = 7 glb (t2).
# (What reads the hole, the lots and the takes over them, is this interpreter's reading of "anchors their sum".)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind funds: unit
kind purchases: event certain
  leg units: funds
kind sales: event certain
  leg units: funds
place h: holdings glb lives 2020-01-01..
place mk: outside lives 2000-01-01..
input bank: observed

fill matched
  supply b.units.amount for b in purchases over ..
  demand x.units.amount for x in sales over ..
  arc b.day <= x.day
  order b.day

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  funds + [glb] lives 2018-01-01..
  opening[h] = 12 glb at 2026-01-01 start "o"
  bank[p1] = (on: 2024-03-01, kind: purchases, leg units from mk to h amount 4 glb) "p1"
  bank[p2] = (on: 2025-03-01, kind: purchases, leg units from mk to h amount 6 glb) "p2"
  bank[s1] = (on: 2026-02-01, kind: sales, leg units from h to mk amount 5 glb) "s1"

ask t1: matched.taken[b, x] for b in purchases over .., x in sales over ..
ask t2: bal(h, 2026-03-01)
=== expect
t1 (b = bank[p1], x = bank[s1]): ?"h: the lots held before 2026-01-01 sum to 10 glb, the opening reading states 12 glb" (h)
  cut 2026-06-30
t1 (b = bank[p2], x = bank[s1]): ?"h: the lots held before 2026-01-01 sum to 10 glb, the opening reading states 12 glb" (h)
  cut 2026-06-30
t2: 7 glb
  cut 2026-06-30
